# RustSS — Cursor rules

The canonical contributor guide is AGENTS.md. Read AGENTS.md, docs/PRD.md,
docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, docs/DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md, and docs/FINDINGS.md before coding.

Project: RustSS — a self-hosted, multi-user, AI-augmented RSS reader in Rust
(Axum + Askama/HTMX, PostgreSQL/pgvector, Redis, background "AGENTS" workers).
It is a ground-up Rust reimplementation of the original `neureed` (Next.js/TS).

THE ONE RULE — never break it:
  Content is shared; state is personal. Feeds/articles/embeddings/summaries are
  stored and computed ONCE and shared across subscribers; per-user data layers on
  top. A feed followed by N users must be O(1) work, not O(N).
  (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §7, docs/PRD.md §6)

Non-negotiables:
- thiserror in libraries, anyhow in bins/agent boundaries. No unwrap()/expect()
  on fallible paths outside tests/startup.
- SQLx compile-checked queries; commit .sqlx/ offline metadata. Per-user queries
  are scoped by user_id; shared writes are idempotent (ON CONFLICT).
- All outbound HTTP goes through SafeFetchClient (SSRF-guarded). No direct reqwest
  to feed/article/robots/media URLs.
- Secrets encrypted with the unified AEAD helper; never log secret material.
- One embedding model per instance; never pad/truncate vectors across dimensions.
- Caching via the Cache port; shared vs per-user key separation; invalidate with
  SCAN/tags, never KEYS.
- Recurring/background work is an Agent run through the framework (scheduler/queue/
  lock/run-record); no ad-hoc tokio::spawn loops.
- Follow the milestone plan in docs/DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md.

When you find a smell/bug/risk, add an entry to docs/FINDINGS.md and reference the
FND-* id in your commit.

Before every commit: cargo fmt --all --check; cargo clippy --all-targets
--all-features -- -D warnings; cargo test. Use Conventional Commits with a body
that explains WHY. Do not push unless asked. Never weaken security to pass CI.
